bly heavier/slower to boot than `nats`/`rabbitmq`, so the generated test needs a readiness-poll loop (not a fixed sleep) and should disable functions-worker/stream-storage to cut startup cost — this is test-code guidance, not a deterministic setup item.\n\n--- human-intervention-logs/org.apache.pulsar:pulsar-client-all:4.2.5/library-preparation-preflight/claude-code-session-c95ptyzj.log ---\n2:You are preparing a Forge workflow for a library issue. Decide whether the library needs setup beyond the normal generated test scaffold before meaningful coverage is reachable.\n6:The setup can be one of three things: an extra Maven dependency, a Docker image the tests need, or an environment/system property the generated tests must set. Represent dependencies and Docker images as `deterministic_setup` entries the driver can apply before generation:\n39:{\"duration_api_ms\":230345,\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"32eba1ed-6dde-4e06-84d8-73579bccf2af\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.6773591999999999,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":34,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":59479,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1091716,\"output_tokens\":16603,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"thinking_tokens\":10492},\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":59479,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":2,\"output_tokens\":1884,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":82377,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1105,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1105},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-sonnet-5\":{\"inputTokens\":34,\"outputTokens\":16603,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1091716,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":59479,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.6223572,\"contextWindow\":1000000,\"maxOutputTokens\":64000,\"thinkingTokens\":10492,\"canonicalModel\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"provider\":\"firstParty\",\"costBasis\":\"list\"},\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":28652,\"outputTokens\":1270,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":2,\"costUSD\":0.055002,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000,\"thinkingTokens\":0,\"canonicalModel\":\"claude-haiku-4-5\",\"provider\":\"firstParty\",\"costBasis\":\"list\"}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"fast_mode_disabled_reason\":\"sdk_opt_in_required\",\"subagent_stats\":{\"spawned\":0,\"requested\":{\"background\":0,\"foreground\":0,\"unset\":0},\"started_in_background\":0,\"max_depth\":0,\"spawned_by_subagents\":0,\"completed\":0,\"failed\":0,\"killed\":{\"parent\":0,\"user\":0,\"system\":0},\"refused\":{\"depth_limit\":0,\"concurrency_limit\":0,\"budget\":0},\"by_type\":{}},\"is_error\":false,\"num_turns\":29,\"subtype\":\"success\",\"api_error_status\":null,\"result\":\"Based on research into `org.apache.pulsar:pulsar-client-all:4.2.5` — the shaded Pulsar Java client used by Spring Pulsar to connect to a broker over `pulsar://host:6650` — here's the decision.\\n\\nKey findings:\\n- `pulsar-client-all` is a self-contained uber-jar; its POM pulls in `pulsar-client-api`, `bouncy-castle-bc`, BouncyCastle, OpenTelemetry, slf4j, etc. as normal transitive Maven deps — Gradle resolves these automatically, so no extra `dependency` entry is needed (same as the existing `io.nats:jnats` and `com.rabbitmq.client` scaffolds, which add only the library coordinate itself).\\n- Meaningful reachability coverage for a messaging client means actually creating a producer/consumer against a live broker — this repo's convention for exactly that situation (`io.nats:jnats`, `com.rabbitmq.client:amqp-client`) is a `required-docker-images.txt` + a `docker run` in the test, backed by a pinned tag under `tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/resources/allowed-docker-images/`. No Pulsar image is pinned there yet.\\n- The official `apachepulsar/pulsar` image runs a full standalone broker (+ BookKeeper + ZooKeeper in one process) via `bin/pulsar standalone`, exposing `6650` (binary protocol) and `8080` (admin HTTP). Tag `4.2.5` exists on Docker Hub and matches the client version exactly (verified against Maven Central's `maven-metadata.xml`, which also confirms `pulsar-client-all:4.2.5` itself is published).\\n- Pulsar standalone is noticeably heavier/slower to boot than `nats`/`rabbitmq`, so the generated test needs a readiness-poll loop (not a fixed sleep) and should disable functions-worker/stream-storage to cut startup cost — this is test-code guidance, not a deterministic setup item.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"action\\\": \\\"advisory_preparation\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"pulsar-client-all needs a live broker for meaningful producer/consumer coverage; no extra Maven dependency required since the uber-jar resolves its own transitives.\\\",\\n  \\\"deterministic_setup\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"kind\\\": \\\"docker_image\\\",\\n      \\\"image\\\": \\\"apachepulsar/pulsar:4.2.5\\\",\\n      \\\"slug\\\": \\\"apachepulsar_pulsar\\\",\\n      \\\"reason\\\": \\\"pulsar-client-all is a network client; exercising producer/consumer/admin paths requires a running Pulsar broker, matching this repo's existing pattern for io.nats:jnats and com.rabbitmq.client:amqp-client. Tag 4.2.5 matches the library version exactly.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"agent_guidance\\\": \\\"Start the container with `bin/pulsar standalone --no-functions-worker --no-stream-storage` to avoid starting the functions worker and BookKeeper-backed stream storage, which aren't needed for basic producer/consumer coverage and would otherwise slow startup. Expose ports 6650 (client serviceUrl `pulsar://localhost:6650`) and 8080 (admin HTTP, usable for readiness polling, e.g. GET /admin/v2/clusters). Pulsar standalone takes substantially longer to become ready than nats/rabbitmq (it boots a broker, bookie, and ZooKeeper in one JVM), so the test must poll/retry for readiness with a generous timeout rather than reuse the short fixed sleep pattern seen in JnatsTest. Tear down the container (docker kill/rm) after the test so repeated local runs don't leak containers.\\\",\\n  \\\"risks\\\": [\\n    \\\"Pulsar standalone's startup is slower and more resource-hungry than the other broker images already allow-listed (nats, rabbitmq), which may increase test wall-clock time and flakiness risk under constrained CI resources.\\\",\\n    \\\"pulsar-client-all is a large shaded jar (~hundreds of MB transitively: netty, avro, protobuf, bouncycastle); native-image build time/memory could be heavier than typical libraries in this repo — no specific blocking GraalVM issue was found during research, but local Gradle/native-image verification remains authoritative.\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"ttft_ms\":9022,\"type\":\"result\",\"duration_ms\":230221,\"uuid\":\"73683c41-408f-4ffe-8b19-427d4a462c9a\",\"ttft_stream_ms\":1797,\"time_to_request_ms\":101,\"first_content_frame_ms\":1797,\"queued_turn_count\":0,\"result_index\":0}\n\n--- human-intervention-logs/org.apache.pulsar:pulsar-client-all:4.2.5/native-test-verify/cycle-0-finalizedTest-2026-10-13T22-53-07-765470Z.log ---\n187:-H:ConfigurationFileDirectories@user=/home/mihailo/git/graalvm-reachability-metadata-worker3/forge/local_repositories/forge_worktrees/10642-c4655eef/tests/src/org.apache.pulsar/pulsar-client-all/4.2.5/build/native/generated/generateTestResourcesConfigFile,/home/mihailo/git/graalvm-reachability-metadata-worker3/forge/local_repositories/forge_worktrees/10642-c4655eef/metadata/org.junit.jupiter/junit-jupiter-api/5.8.2,/home/mihailo/git/graalvm-reachability-metadata-worker3/forge/local_repositories/forge_worktrees/10642-c4655eef/metadata/org.opentest4j/opentest4j/1.2.0,/home/mihailo/git/graalvm-reachability-metadata-worker3/forge/local_repositories/forge_worktrees/10642-c4655eef/metadata/org.junit.platform/junit-platform-commons/1.8.2,/home/mihailo/git